        "date": "2026-03-06T12:26:20Z"
      },
      "message": "unprivileged/integrated-matrix: Use tile-strided scale layout in v0 for microscaling\n\nReplace the contiguous scale layout (index = m × S + s) with a\ntile-strided layout (index = m × R + s, where R = λ × SEW ÷ 16).\nThis distributes scale data naturally across hardware lanes in\nmulti-lane implementations.\n\nKey changes:\n- Introduce row stride R with M × R = VLEN ÷ 16 (scales always fill\n  exactly one register regardless of configuration)\n- Add R ≥ S proof for both block sizes (32 and 16)\n- Update capacity table with R column\n- Update SAIL index expressions in all three FP multiply-accumulate\n  instructions (vfmmacc.vv, vfqwmmacc.vv, vfwmmacc.vv)\n- Restructure scale-packing examples with new pre-paired load options\n  (vmtl.v and vle16.v) and renumber existing options\n\nWhen S = R (maximum K_eff case), the layout is identical to the\nprevious contiguous layout.  When S < R, padding positions within\neach row stride are don't-care.",
